[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807619869","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105441#issuecomment-2807619869","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105441","id":2807619869,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nWOEd","user":{"login":"Sch1nken","id":11414422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDE0NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11414422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken","html_url":"https://github.com/Sch1nken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T21:57:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T21:57:09Z","body":"`but was found while trying to inspect a Node that had aforementioned type of dictionary as a property.`\nI've reported a similiar issue (at least concerning the inspector issues). For me it happened when I was using a custom class_name as Key. If I used the extended class as Key everything is fine. \n\nMight be related (to an extend?)\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105374","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807619869/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807662509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105441#issuecomment-2807662509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105441","id":2807662509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nWYet","user":{"login":"FlowerLover32","id":118894576,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxYv8A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118894576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32","html_url":"https://github.com/FlowerLover32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T22:23:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T22:25:38Z","body":"> `but was found while trying to inspect a Node that had aforementioned type of dictionary as a property.` I've reported a similiar issue (at least concerning the inspector issues). For me it happened when I was using a custom class_name as Key. If I used the extended class as Key everything is fine.\n> \n> Might be related (to an extend?) [#105374](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105374)\n\nIn #105374, You create a custom Class (PremiumColorRect) that extends a built-in godot class (ColorRect), and add it as a key in an entry. only then add it as a child.\n\nIn this issue, I create a Node and add it as a child, and then add it as a key in an entry, which seems to work fine, until that Node is freed. (based on my tests, changing Node to anything that extends Node works just the same)\n\nIf they are related, it appears that an issue might be related to transition of the Node out of and into the tree, to an extent.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807662509/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2809725243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105441#issuecomment-2809725243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105441","id":2809725243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6neQE7","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T14:12:47Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T14:12:47Z","body":"I'd say this is pretty expected, freed nodes are different, and accessing the value is unsafe\n\nIf you need to be able to handle these nodes being freed you should probably use object IDs instead, using [`get_instance_id`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-get-instance-id), and using [`instance_from_id`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40globalscope.html#class-globalscope-method-instance-from-id)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2809725243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2811310277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105441#issuecomment-2811310277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105441","id":2811310277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nkTDF","user":{"login":"FlowerLover32","id":118894576,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxYv8A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118894576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32","html_url":"https://github.com/FlowerLover32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlowerLover32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T00:23:23Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T00:23:23Z","body":"> I'd say this is pretty expected, freed nodes are different, and accessing the value is unsafe\n> \n> If you need to be able to handle these nodes being freed you should probably use object IDs instead, using [`get_instance_id`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-get-instance-id), and using [`instance_from_id`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40globalscope.html#class-globalscope-method-instance-from-id)\n\nI only think that no matter if the user is doing dumb code, they should still be able to use the built-in functionality, such as the inspector\nThanks for advice by the way! I'll look into it, and likely use it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2811310277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]